pronunciation between the singular ''woman'' and the plural ''women'', though it has come to distinguish the singular from the plural, is entirely accidental; formerly both pronunciations of the first syllable were in use in both numbers. The proper modern spelling of the plural, as now pronounced, would be ''wimmen;'' the spelling ''women'' is due to irreg. conformity to the singular ''woman'', which is properly so spelled according to the analogy of ''wolf'', though *''wooman'', like *''woolf'', would be better, as being then in keeping with ''wool'', ''wood''<sup>1</sup>.] '''1.''' An adult female of the human race; figuratively, the female sex; human females collectively. See ''lady'', 5.
{{smaller block|<poem>Leode [men] nere thar nane,
ne wapmen ne ''wifmen'',
bute westiȝe [waste] paedes.</poem>
{{right|''Layamon'', l. 1119.}}
That is the Lond of Femynye, where that no man is, but only alle ''Wommen''. {{right|''Mandeville'', Travels, p. 143.}}
Whan the queene vndirstode the a-vow that Gawein hadde made, she was the gladdest ''woman'' in the worlde.
{{right|''Merlin'' (E. E. T. S.), iii. 483.}}
